PROP-108 Phase 1 enforce mode — flipped 2026-07-01T06:00:00Z by operator.

Rationale:
- Mechanism is zero-risk to enforce: directive-auto-close.js can only close a directive
  whose linked PROP is in the whitelist AND whose linkage resolves. Missing linkage = no-op.
- PROP-120 (integrated 2026-06-30) added the auto_close_when_deliverable_proposed opt-in
  for propose-only authoring directives, plus RC2 back-ref backfill for PROP-113/PROP-114.
- ~20 zombie directives currently pending; most lack directive_id back-refs on their
  fulfilling PROP. Enforce mode alone can't reach them — DIRECTIVE-20260701-001 (parallel
  commission) asks tinker to audit + propose backfills, at which point the mechanism
  will drain them mechanically each tinker run.
- Sibling: PROP-102 (prop-auto-close-enforce.flag) remains at operator discretion — this
  flag is directive-only.

If auto-close causes an incorrect closure, delete this flag file to revert to shadow mode.
The prior shadow-mode ledger (monitor/tinker/directive-auto-close-ledger.jsonl) records
every dryrun would-close decision, so any bad closure can be traced + reversed via the
CLAUDE.md DIRECTIVE-LIFECYCLE additive-edit exception (pending → completed transition
allowed exactly once, so mis-closed directives are recoverable by resetting to pending
and re-processing).
